{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773873096,"nonce":"Vtv+MPA/uVZlfS0A6q+L6yEABAo=","title":"Audit repo history for ToS-sensitive OAuth/SDK setup before public release","message":"Before making this repo public, audit the git history for any content that describes or facilitates using Claude Code OAuth credentials in an unsanctioned way (e.g. third-party use of the claude-agent-sdk authenticated via stolen/reused Claude Code OAuth tokens rather than an official API key).\n\nConcerns:\n- The @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk is authenticated by reading Claude Codes stored OAuth credentials (~/.claude/credentials or similar). Using this in a third-party application is almost certainly outside the intended ToS scope for Claude Code OAuth.\n- Any code comments, setup instructions, or commit messages that explain HOW to configure this (e.g. pointing to credential file locations, explaining the OAuth token reuse pattern) are effectively a ToS circumvention tutorial once the repo is public.\n- Credentials themselves should never be committed (likely clean already), but the pattern documentation is the real risk.\n\nWhat needs to be audited:\n1. sdk-backend.ts and surrounding code for comments explaining OAuth credential sourcing\n2. Any CLAUDE.md, README, or docs commits that describe the setup\n3. Commit messages across the feature/sdk-backend branch\n4. Whether the SDK integration should be gated behind a standard API key path for public use, with the OAuth path either removed or undocumented\n\nMitigation options (in order of least to most annoying):\nA. Document publicly only the API-key path; ensure OAuth path is behind a compile flag or env var with no public documentation\nB. Rewrite history with git filter-repo to remove sensitive commits (moderate pain — rewrites all hashes, breaks any existing clones, invalidates Mandible auth request hash references in SQLite)\nC. Start a fresh public repo from a clean export, keeping this repo private (most annoying for ongoing workflow but cleanest separation)\n\nThis should be resolved before any public release. Not urgent for private use.","files":null}]}